<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Disabled is asserted; Outputs OFF; Run Status shown but Alarms disabled]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Labels/>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_Start)OTU(PCmd_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Start) OTU(OCmd_Stop) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Commands or Settings, we're not READY for any of them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_Start) OTU(Rdy_Stop) ,OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) OTU(Rdy_Disable) OTU(Rdy_Enable) ,OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Running Status (Sts_Running) bit shows if the Motor is running,
even though the Motor is Disabled by being on a false rung.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Running) OTE(Sts_Running) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Starting) OTE(Sts_Starting) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Stopping) OTE(Sts_Stopping) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Stopped Status (Sts_Stopped) bit shows if the Motor is stopped,
even though the Motor is Disabled by being on a false rung.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Sts_Running)XIO(Sts_Starting)XIO(Sts_Stopping)OTE(Sts_Stopped);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The remaining actual Motor status bits are passed through to Status,
even though the Motor is Disabled by being on a false rung.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_AtSpeed) OTE(Sts_AtSpeed) ,[XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Enabled) ,XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Ready) ] OTE(Sts_NotReady) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Fdbk is the current state of the device feedback, as seen on the AOI's Inputs:
0 = Stopped
1 = Running
3 = Starting
4 = Stopping]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Stopped) CLR(Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_Running) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_Starting) MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_Stopping) MOV(4,Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On powerup (prescan), set Motor to stop.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_Run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset the fault condition and simulation / command retrigger timers.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_StartT)RES(Wrk_StopT)RES(Wrk_StartRetrigT)RES(Wrk_StopRetrigT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs are cleared on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MVM(0,16#0000_001f,Out.LogicCommand);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REMAINING MOTOR VALUES AND STATUS
============================================================
This rung calculates or copies Values and Status for the Motor
from their Input values (with decimal shifting as appropriate).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[DIV(Inp.CurrentPhaseA,10.0,Val_CurPhaseA) DIV(Inp.CurrentPhaseB,10.0,Val_CurPhaseB) DIV(Inp.CurrentPhaseC,10.0,Val_CurPhaseC) ,NEQ(Inp.FullLoadAmps,0.0) CPT(Val_AvgPctFLA,(Val_CurPhaseA+Val_CurPhaseB+Val_CurPhaseC)/3.0/Inp.FullLoadAmps*10.0) ,EQU(Inp.FullLoadAmps,0.0) CLR(Val_AvgPctFLA) ,MOV(Inp.WattMeter,Val_RealPwr) DIV(Inp.PowerFactor,100.0,Val_PwrFact) MOV(Inp.MtrThermUsage,Val_PctTherm) ,NEQ(Inp.FaultCode1,0) MOV(Inp.FaultCode1,Val_LastFaultCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Motor does not show faulted in EnableInFalse, so clear the Val_FaultDesc string.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Val_FaultDesc,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the drive as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available, and with no
Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb.
Clear speed reference and output datalink values.
Show the enumerated drive command as NONE.
Show the enumerated drive status as DISABLED.
Show the enumberated drive fault status as NONE, except show
as CONFIG ERR if there is a configuration error.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_Disabled) OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) OTU(Nrdy_Disabled) OTU(Nrdy_Intlk) OTU(Nrdy_Perm) ,OTU(Nrdy_DriveNR) OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_FailToStart) OTU(Alm_FailToStop) OTU(Alm_IntlkTrip) OTU(Alm_MotorFault) OTU(Alm_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_FailToStart) OTU(Sts_FailToStop) OTU(Sts_IntlkTrip) OTU(Sts_MotorFault) OTU(Sts_IOFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan: control / monitor Motor via SMCFlex Smart Starter]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Labels>
<Label Name="SkipText"/>
</Labels>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_SMCFlex :  PROCESS -- SMCFlex Smart Motor Controller
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30.  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V3.1-00  2014-07-15:  Initial Release (Part of Library of Process Objects V3.1, so Major = 3).
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed jog, fail timers ACC/PRE (read-only). Corrections to Nrdy_
trip and reset logic. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode 3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction controls and monitors a motor via an SMCFlex
Smart Starter and provides:

*  Starting, stopping of the motor
*  Monitoring of run feedback, display of actual motor status
*  Detection of Failure to Start, Failure to Stop, Motor/Starter Fault
*  Monitoring of Permissive conditions to allow starting
* Monitoring of Interlock conditions to stop / prevent starting
* Simulation, providing feedback of a working motor and starter while disabling outputs
* Monitoring of I/O communication faults
* Alarms for Fail to Start, Fail to Stop, Interlock Trip, Motor / Starter Fault, I/O Fault
* Option to automatically reset faults and alarms when operator commands
motor to start or stop
* Supports HMI "breadcrumbs" for Alarm Inhibited, Bad Configuration,
Not Ready, Maintenance Bypass Active
* "Available" status for use by automation logic to know whether motor
can be controlled by other objects.

Modes are provided by a P_Mode Add-On Instruction instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm Add-On Instruction instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand

See Rockwell Automation Publication 150-UM008_-EN-P for
information on SMCFlex Smart Starter parameters and programming.
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)CONCAT(Val_FaultDesc,Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs get Configuration data (such as timer presets) and distribute as needed.
Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

Enter the time (in seconds) for the Motor to successfully start before declaring a fault.
Enter the time (in seconds) for the Motor to successfully stop before declaring a fault.
Enter the time (in seconds) for the Motor Fault Reset output to be pulsed when a reset is received.
(The reset pulse time is also used for pulsing Start or Stop
output on a start or stop command retrigger in Maintenance.)

If the timer preset calcuated wraps negative (more than 2.14... million seconds), then max out the
or clear the Timer Preset (as appropriate) and flag it.  Note that a negative timer preset will fault the controller!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[MUL(Cfg_FailToStartT,1000,Wrk_StartT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_StartT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_StartT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_FailToStopT,1000,Wrk_StopT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_StopT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_StopT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_ResetPulseT,1000,Wrk_ResetT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_ResetT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_ResetT.PRE) ] OTE(Err_Timer) ,MOV(Wrk_ResetT.PRE,Wrk_StartRetrigT.PRE) MOV(Wrk_ResetT.PRE,Wrk_StopRetrigT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the reports of all Bad Configuration Status.
Individual bits are provided for various status:
Bad Raw Scaling configs
Bad Engineering Units Scaling configs
Bad Min or Max Speed Reference clamp limit
Bad simulation speed ramp time
Bad timer config from (rung above)
Bad Alarm config (from P_Alarm)
Bad Cfg_OperKeep / Cfg_ProgKeep config

Then a summary Bad Config status is provided, simply an OR of the individual bits.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_SimFdbkT,0) OTE(Err_Sim) ,XIC(Err_Timer) ,[XIC(FailToStart.Sts_Err) ,XIC(FailToStop.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_Err) ,XIC(MotorFault.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
RUN FEEDBACK PROCESSING
============================================================
If the device is being simulated or has no feedback,
use the simulation timers to provide "fake" feedback.

If the motor is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING a run feedback,
use the state of the run feedback input as the motor run state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Wrk_StartRetrigT.DN) OTL(Wrk_RunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_StopRetrigT.DN) OTU(Wrk_RunFdbk) ] ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Running) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Stopping) ] OTL(Wrk_RunFdbk) ,[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Starting) ,XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Running) XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Stopping) XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Starting) ] OTU(Wrk_RunFdbk) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung copies the Motor Status Word bits to external Status parameters of the instruction.
When this instruction is in simulation, simulated status is generated to "act like" a Motor.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Enabled) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTE(Sts_CtrlPwrOK) ,[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Phasing) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTE(Sts_Phasing) ,[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_PhasingActive) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTE(Sts_PhasingActive) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Alarm) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_Alarm) ,[XIO(Inp_Sim) XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_AtSpeed) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) XIC(Wrk_Run) XIC(Wrk_RunFdbk) ] OTE(Sts_AtSpeed) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_StartIsol) OTE(Sts_StartIsol) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Bypass) OTE(Sts_ExtBypass) ,XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Ready) OTE(Sts_NotReady) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Opt1Inp) OTE(Sts_Opt1Inp) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Opt2Inp) OTE(Sts_Opt2Inp) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Fdbk is the current state of the device feedback, as seen on the AOI's Inputs:
0 = Stopped
1 = Running
3 = Accelerating
4 = Decelerating]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Stopped) CLR(Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_Running) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_Starting) MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_Stopping) MOV(4,Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INTERLOCK / PERMISSIVE BYPASS / CHECK COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Bypass Command bypasses the Bypassable Permissives and Interlocks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Bypass)OTU(OCmd_Bypass)OTL(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Check Command enables checking of ALL
Permissives and Interlocks (cancels the bypass).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Check)OTU(OCmd_Check)OTU(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected OR in Maintenance Mode,
or in Override Mode if Override Bypassing is configured.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Ovrd) XIC(Cfg_OvrdPermIntlk) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ]OTE(Sts_BypActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Interlock / Permissive Bypass function is enabled
*  Motor HAS run feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE run feedback]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Bypass)OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready for Interlock / Permissive Bypass if not bypassed.
Ready to cancel Bypass (resume checking) if bypassed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Bypass) ,XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Check) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE DISABLE/ENABLE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Disable Command disables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Disable)OTU(MCmd_Disable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTL(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Enable Command cancels the Disable and enables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Enable)OTU(MCmd_Enable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTU(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Disabled flag is set, the Motor is DISABLED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Disabled)OTE(Sts_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to Disable device if in Maintenance Mode and device is NOT Disabled.
Ready to Enable device if in Maintenance Mode and device IS Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)[XIO(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Disable) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input
4.  Resets initiated by other device Operator Commands (if configured to do so)

and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

The reset starts the Reset Timer (One-Shot Off-Delay)
to ensure the output is held on for at least the minimum time.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,[XIC(OCmd_Start) ,XIC(OCmd_Stop) ] XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) [XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(FailToStart.PCmd_Ack) ,OTL(FailToStop.PCmd_Ack) ,OTL(MotorFault.PCmd_Ack) ,OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Ack) ,OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Ack) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ONS(Wrk_ResetONS) ][OTL(FailToStart.PCmd_Reset) OTL(FailToStop.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Sts_FailToStart) RES(Wrk_StartT) ,XIC(Sts_FailToStop) RES(Wrk_StopT) ,OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) ,[XIO(Inp_IOFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,TOF(Wrk_ResetT,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Hold Timer "done" bit comes on immediately and stays on
for the hold time.  If it, or any held-on reset initiator, is TRUE, set the Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_ResetT.DN)[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Fault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Out.LogicCommand_ClearFaults) ,OTL(MotorFault.PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR START / STOP COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Motor is NOT READY TO RUN if:
* Interlocks are not OK and not bypassed;
* Non-bypassable Interlocks are not OK;
* Permissives are not OK and not bypassed,
or Non-Bypassable Permissives are not OK, 
and the motor is not already starting or running;
* The Motor (not simulated) reports that it is faulted;
* There's an I/O failure and the motor is NOT being simulated;
* The motor has a Fail to Start that has not been reset;
* The Motor is disabled (by Maintenance);
* This instruction instance has a configuration error.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_NoMode)[XIC(Sts_Disabled) OTE(Nrdy_Disabled) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,[XIO(Inp_IntlkOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_NBIntlkOK) ] [XIC(Wrk_Run) OTE(Sts_IntlkTrip) ,OTE(Nrdy_Intlk) ] ,[XIO(Inp_PermOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_NBPermOK) ] XIO(Sts_Starting) XIO(Sts_Running) OTE(Nrdy_Perm) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Fault) OTE(Sts_MotorFault) OTE(Nrdy_Trip) ,[XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Ready) XIO(Out.LogicCommand_Stop) ,XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Enabled) ] OTE(Nrdy_DriveNR) ] ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_IOFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnIOFault) OTL(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Wrk_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR START / STOP COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Motor is NOT READY TO RUN if:
* Interlocks are not OK and not bypassed;
* Non-bypassable Interlocks are not OK;
* Permissives are not OK and not bypassed,
or Non-Bypassable Permissives are not OK, 
and the motor is not already starting or running;
* The Motor (not simulated) reports that it is faulted;
* There's an I/O failure and the motor is NOT being simulated;
* The motor has a Fail to Start that has not been reset;
* The Motor is disabled (by Maintenance);
* This instruction instance has a configuration error.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ,XIC(Nrdy_OperPrio) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The motor is AVAILABLE to be run by automation if it is in PROGRAM
Mode and the "Not Ready" status is cleared.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Sts_Prog)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Sts_Available);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If we're not timing an HMI or programmed Start or Stop,
and there's no sealed-in fail-to-start or fail-to-stop,
and if Local Start/Stop Control is permitted,
and if we are using run feedback (not in simulation),
detect a local start or stop transition and track state with it.
(Don't track the Start if conditions do not allow the motor to run.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_StartT.TT)XIO(Wrk_StopT.TT)XIO(Sts_FailToStart)XIO(Sts_FailToStop)XIC(Cfg_AllowLocal)XIO(Inp_Sim)[[XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Running) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Starting) ] XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Stopping) XIO(Sts_NotRdy) OTL(Wrk_Run) ,[XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Running) XIO(Inp.LogicStatus_Starting) ,XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Stopping) ] OTU(Wrk_Run) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These next several rungs, in priority order, determine whether
the Motor should be running, jogging or stopped.

If a Motor START command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is RUN, mark the Motor to RUN.
Permissives must be OK or bypassed to start the Motor (Interlocks are checked below...).
(Modes are mutually exclusive, thus handling the priority.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Start) OTU(OCmd_Start) [XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Start) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Start) ,NOP() ] XIC(Mode.Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,2) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Mode.Sts_Ovrd) ]XIO(Sts_NotRdy)[[XIO(Wrk_Run) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ] OTL(Wrk_Retrigger) RES(Wrk_StartRetrigT) ,OTL(Wrk_Run) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Motor STOP command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is STOP,
mark the Motor TO STOP.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Stop) OTU(OCmd_Stop) [XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_OperStopPrio) XIO(Mode.Sts_Oper) XIO(Mode.Sts_Maint) OTL(Nrdy_OperPrio) ] ,[XIC(PCmd_Stop) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Stop) ,NOP() ] ,XIO(PCmd_Start) XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear) ] XIC(Mode.Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,1) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Mode.Sts_Ovrd) ,XIC(Sts_NotRdy) ][[XIC(Wrk_Run) ,ONS(Wrk_NotRdyONS) ] OTL(Wrk_Retrigger) RES(Wrk_StopRetrigT) ,OTU(Wrk_Run) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Higher Priority: HAND wins over other Modes:
If in Hand, have the Motor follow the RunFeedback.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Mode.Sts_Hand) ,XIC(S:FS) ]XIO(Sts_NotRdy)[XIC(Wrk_RunFdbk) OTL(Wrk_Run) ,XIO(Wrk_RunFdbk) OTU(Wrk_Run) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR START RETRIGGER AND FAIL TO START DETECTION
============================================================
If the Motor SHOULD BE RUNNING, run a Start Timer to check for Fail to Start,
 and run a Retrigger timer to pulse the Start output if needed.

@@@@@  The TON on the second branch is doubled to ensure it goes  @@@@@
@@@@@  the same scan it is enabled if its preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Run)[XIO(Wrk_RunFdbk) TON(Wrk_StartT,?,?) ,TON(Wrk_StartRetrigT,?,?) TON(Wrk_StartRetrigT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_StartRetrigT.DN) OTU(Wrk_Retrigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Start Timer times out and the motor run feedback (or simulated feedback) never showed up,
show the motor as "FAILED TO START"]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_StartT.DN)XIO(Mode.Sts_Maint)OTE(Sts_FailToStart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MOTOR STOP RETRIGGER AND FAIL TO STOP DETECTION
============================================================
If the Motor SHOULD BE STOPPED, run a Stop Timer to check for Fail to Stop,
 and run a Retrigger timer to pulse the Stop output if needed.

@@@@@  The TON on the second branch is doubled to ensure it goes  @@@@@
@@@@@  the same scan it is enabled if its preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_Run)[XIC(Wrk_RunFdbk) TON(Wrk_StopT,?,?) ,TON(Wrk_StopRetrigT,?,?) TON(Wrk_StopRetrigT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_StopRetrigT.DN) OTU(Wrk_Retrigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Stop Timer times out and the motor run feedback (or simulated feedback)
never showed "stopped", show the motor as "FAILED TO STOP"]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_StopT.DN)XIO(Mode.Sts_Maint)OTE(Sts_FailToStop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SHED ON FAULT LOGIC
============================================================
This rung handles latching in of conditions which are configured to cause
Motor to shed (de-energize).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_FailToStart)XIC(Cfg_ShedOnFailToStart)OTL(Nrdy_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a shed condition is latched in above, de-energize the Motor.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Nrdy_OperPrio) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTU(Wrk_Run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE COMMAND ENUMERATED VALUE
============================================================
Val_Cmd is the command currently being processed:
0 = None
1 = Stop
2 = Start]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Cmd) ,XIO(Wrk_Run) [XIC(Wrk_RunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Wrk_Run) [XIO(Wrk_RunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] MOV(2,Wrk_Cmd) ,MOV(Wrk_Cmd,Val_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT GENERATION
============================================================
If the Motor is NOT SIMULATED and NOT LOCALLY CONTROLLED,\
generate the appropriate outputs for the Motor.

If the Motor should be running, is not faulted and not in hardwired control, energize Out_Run.
Also, energize Out_Start until we get feedback that the Motor is running.

If the Motor should be stopped and is not in hardwired control and the feedback shows the Motor
is NOT stopped, or if the Motor is Faulted, energize the Out_Stop output to stop the Motor.

Finally, if the Motor is not simulated, energize the appropriate direction output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Mode.Sts_Hand)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) XIC(Wrk_Run) [XIO(Wrk_RunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ] OTE(Out.LogicCommand_Start) ,XIO(Wrk_Run) [XIC(Wrk_RunFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Retrigger) ,XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ] OTE(Out.LogicCommand_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates the Starting, Running, Stopping, Stopped and Jogging Status bits.

If the Motor is in HAND and HAS NO RUN FEEDBACK, its state is meaningless;
turn off ALL the Sts_xxx states!!!!!

If the Motor is commanded to run (Output on) and the feedback doesn't yet show it running,
the Motor is STARTING.

If the Motor is commanded to run (Output on) and the feedback shows it running,
the Motor is RUNNING.

If the Motor is commanded to stoop (Output off) and the feedback still shows it running,
the Motor is STOPPING.

If the Motor is commanded to stop (Output off) and the feedback shows it has stopped,
the Motor is STOPPED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Run) [XIO(Wrk_RunFdbk) OTE(Sts_Starting) ,XIC(Wrk_RunFdbk) OTE(Sts_Running) ] ,XIO(Wrk_Run) [XIC(Wrk_RunFdbk) OTE(Sts_Stopping) ,XIO(Wrk_RunFdbk) OTE(Sts_Stopped) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Sts is the current device status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = Powerup / Unknown (Hand Mode with no feedback, for example)
1 = Stopped
2 = Running Forward
3 = Running Reverse
4 = Jogging Forward
5 = Jogging Reverse
6 = Stopping
7 = Starting Forward
8 = Starting Reverse
33 = Device Disabled

Val_Fault is the current device fault status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the fault status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = None
16 = Fail to Start
17 = Fail to Stop
18 = Motor Fault
32 = I/O Fault (from Input)
34 = Configuration Error]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Sts) CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Stopped) MOV(1,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Running) MOV(2,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Stopping) MOV(6,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Starting) MOV(7,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_FailToStop) MOV(17,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_MotorFault) MOV(18,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) MOV(32,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Disabled) MOV(33,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================
Ready to Start if in Operator Manual, Stopped, and Permissives and Interlocks are OK.

Ready to Stop if in Operator Manual (or Operator has priority stop) and (Running or Starting).

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_NotRdy)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ,XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ][[XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ] [XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Enabled) XIC(Inp.LogicStatus_Ready) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] [XIC(Sts_Stopped) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) XIC(Sts_Running) ] OTE(Rdy_Start) ,[XIC(Mode.Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Mode.Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_OperStopPrio) ] XIO(Sts_Stopping) OTE(Rdy_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REMAINING MOTOR VALUES AND STATUS
============================================================
This rung calculates or copies Values and Status for the Motor
from their Input values (with decimal shifting as appropriate).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[DIV(Inp.CurrentPhaseA,10.0,Val_CurPhaseA) DIV(Inp.CurrentPhaseB,10.0,Val_CurPhaseB) DIV(Inp.CurrentPhaseC,10.0,Val_CurPhaseC) ,NEQ(Inp.FullLoadAmps,0.0) CPT(Val_AvgPctFLA,(Val_CurPhaseA+Val_CurPhaseB+Val_CurPhaseC)/3.0/Inp.FullLoadAmps*10.0) ,EQU(Inp.FullLoadAmps,0.0) CLR(Val_AvgPctFLA) ,MOV(Inp.WattMeter,Val_RealPwr) DIV(Inp.PowerFactor,100.0,Val_PwrFact) MOV(Inp.MtrThermUsage,Val_PctTherm) ,NEQ(Inp.FaultCode1,0) MOV(Inp.FaultCode1,Val_LastFaultCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Motor is Faulted, this rung finds the Fault Description for
the given Fault Code within the Reference Fault Code List 
(In/Out Parameter).  (The same SMC-Flex Fault Code List
can be referenced by ALL instances of this instruction!!!)

1.  Find the number of entries in the Fault Code List (Array SIZE).
2.  Search (FSC) the Fault Code List for a matching Code.
3.  If found, copy the corresponding Description to Val_FaultDesc.
4.  If NOT found, copy list entry zero ("No Help Available for this code").

And if the Motor is not faulted, clear the Val_FaultDesc string.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_MotorFault) [RES(Wrk_FaultDescFSC) SIZE(Ref_FaultCodeList,0,Wrk_FaultDescFSC.LEN) ,FSC(Wrk_FaultDescFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_FaultCodeList[Wrk_FaultDescFSC.POS].Code=Val_LastFaultCode) ,XIC(Wrk_FaultDescFSC.FD) COP(Ref_FaultCodeList[Wrk_FaultDescFSC.POS].Desc,Val_FaultDesc,1) ,XIO(Wrk_FaultDescFSC.FD) COP(Ref_FaultCodeList[0].Desc,Val_FaultDesc,1) ] ,XIO(Sts_MotorFault) FLL(0,Val_FaultDesc,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SrcQ_IO,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(FailToStart.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(FailToStop.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IntlkTrip.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(MotorFault.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IOFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1).
(The SMC-Flex interface always includes run feedback and Motor fault status.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTL(FailToStart.PCfg_AllowExist)OTL(FailToStop.PCfg_AllowExist)OTL(IntlkTrip.PCfg_AllowExist)OTL(MotorFault.PCfg_AllowExist)OTL(IOFault.PCfg_AllowExist);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Motor Failed to Start Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(FailToStart);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Motor Failed to Stop Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(FailToStop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Interlock Trip Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IntlkTrip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Motor Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(MotorFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle I/O Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(FailToStart.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(FailToStop.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(MotorFault.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Highest severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Highest severity alarm, unacknowledged]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(FailToStart.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(FailToStart.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(FailToStop.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(FailToStop.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(MotorFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(MotorFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(FailToStart.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(FailToStop.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(MotorFault.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IOFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if a latched Shed condition requires a reset in order to run the motor;
* if that reset or any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(FailToStart.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(FailToStop.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(MotorFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(FailToStart.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(FailToStop.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(MotorFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_Trip) ,XIC(Nrdy_OperPrio) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) XIO(Sts_IOFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear Ownership, set motor to STOP, clear "lurking" Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Labels/>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, set the Ownership to NO OWNER (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(PSet_Owner)CLR(Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_Start)OTU(PCmd_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Start) OTU(OCmd_Stop) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On powerup (prescan), set Motor to stop.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_Run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset the fault condition Shed latches.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio)OTU(Nrdy_Fail)OTU(Nrdy_IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs are cleared on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MVM(0,16#0000_001f,Out.LogicCommand);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the enumerated Motor command as NONE.
Show the enumerated Motor feedback as NONE.
Show the enumerated Motor status as POWERUP / UNKNOWN.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Fdbk)CLR(Val_Sts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
<Tags Use="Context">
